<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12734" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκαίω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκαθ-κάω</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέκηα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έκαυσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					25.95
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Philippid.
				25.4
			</span></i>:—<i>burn off,</i> of cautery, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.2.54
			</span></i>, D.l.c.; of intense cold, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύελλαν ἥ κεν ἀπὸ Τρώων κεφαλὰς . .
					κήαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.336
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμος βορρᾶς . . ἀποκαίων πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					4.5.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέκαυσεν ἡ πάχνη τοὺς ἀμπέλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philippid.
				</span></i>
			 l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.3.1
			</span></i>, al.:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεκαίοντο αἱ ῥῖνες</span>
			their noses <i>were frozen off,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.4.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>calcine,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.125
			</span></i>.</div>
